//? Title: CIFAR-10 CNN: RGB Inputs, Augmentation and Explicit Training
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Tiny colour images require joint spatial and channel features, while limited training data
can make a classifier sensitive to image placement. We preview original CIFAR-10 RGB images,
check label-preserving augmentation and train a two-block CNN with an explicit Adam loop.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/cnn_cifar10.cpp`.

> The method

The architecture is SAME Conv(32,3)-ReLU-pool, Conv(64,3)-ReLU-pool, Dense(128)-ReLU,
then ten logits. It retains 8×8×64 features before flattening and has 545098 parameters.
An independent four-pixel zero pad, random 32×32 crop and horizontal flip is drawn for each
training image. Only afterwards pixels map from [0,1] to [-1,1], so padded black becomes -1.
Validation and test images are normalised but never augmented.

$$
J(\theta)=\mathbb E_{(x,y),T}\left[-\log p_\theta(y\mid T(x))\right]
+\frac{10^{-4}}2\sum_{W\text{ kernels}}\|W\|_F^2.
$$
\alttext(The supervised objective averages over label-preserving random transforms and applies kernel L2 regularisation.)

The visible minibatch loop samples transforms and computes tensor cross entropy before each
Adam update. Augmentation is an assumption about label-preserving variation, not a guarantee
for arbitrary images. Use O(B Ho Wo k² Cin Cout) convolution work per layer. This report fits
256 rows from original binary training batch one, validates on the following 64, and evaluates
the first 128 official test images after two epochs. These small fixed subsets illustrate
workflow, not the original full-data accuracy claim. Cached binary CIFAR-10 is required.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/cnn_cifar10_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/cnn_cifar10_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/cnn_cifar10_concept.tikz > build/cnn_cifar10_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/cnn_cifar10_concept.svg build/cnn_cifar10_concept.dvi > build/cnn_cifar10_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
